      "source_type": "drug_general",
      "title": "Ibuprofen",
      "text": "Ibuprofen is a monocarboxylic acid that is propionic acid in which one of the hydrogens at position 2 is substituted by a 4-(2-methylpropyl)phenyl group. It has a role as a geroprotector, a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug, a non-narcotic analgesic, an antipyretic, a xenobiotic, a radical scavenger, a cyclooxygenase 2 inhibitor, a cyclooxygenase 1 inhibitor, an environmental contaminant and a drug allergen. It is functionally related to a propionic acid. It is a conjugate acid of an ibuprofen(1-).",
      "chunk_index": 0,
